    {
     "name": "pattern",
     "type": "list[BlockSpec] | None",
     "required": false,
     "default": null
    }
   ],
   "doc": "Token embedding, `n_layers` copies of `block`, a final norm and the output head.\n\n`pattern=[a, b]` instead of `block` repeats a list of block specs through the layers\n(a, b, a, b, ...), e.g. sliding-window and global attention layers.\n`pos_emb` (e.g. LearnedPosition()) is added after the token embedding; leave it out when\nattention carries the positions (RoPE). Like every model it returns logits, or\n`(logits, aux_loss)` when `z_loss` is set: the z-loss keeps the softmax normaliser near 1.\nBiases start at zero and matrices at N(0, 0.02), and each layer's output projections at\n0.02 / sqrt(2 * n_layers) so the residual stream does not grow with depth.",
   "reference": null,
   "features": [
    "tie_weights",
    "z_loss"
   ],
